Clamp SplashClip coordinates before converting them to integer bounds.

xMaxI/yMaxI are computed as splashCeil(v) - 1. For a clip coordinate outside the
int range (here a W clip under "1 1000000 0 792 1 3 cm" gave yMax = -4.06e11)
the double -> int conversion is undefined (UBSan: "SplashMath.h:122:29: runtime
error: -4.0608e+11 is outside the range of representable values of type 'int'");
x86 and wasm both yield INT_MIN, and the "- 1" wraps it to INT_MAX, so an empty
clip became unbounded. SplashClip::clipToPath() then built a SplashXPathScanner
over ~760M rows: std::length_error from allIntersections.resize() on wasm32,
a ~18 GB allocation on 64-bit. Also check the antialiased yMaxAA multiplication
for overflow, like yMinAA already is.

Regression test cpp/tests/poppler-splashclip-bounds-test.cpp renders a page
whose first clip lies at y ~ 5e9 and fails every operator new above 256 MB
(1.9 GB without the fix).

Not fixed upstream as of d828315.
Upstream: open umbrella issue poppler/poppler#1764 (by LingMaple, 2026-07-20) covers float-to-int overflows; merged !2325 (2026-08-08, in the pin) fixed SplashClip::clipToPath only.
The SplashClip constructor/resetToRect casts fixed here are not covered upstream.

